{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7EHcKp4Gv4b2Bov7rb9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The update is below. It's about 440 words, not counting the subject line.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: [Company] quarterly update: flat revenue, losing our largest customer, and what's next\n\nHi all,\n\nFirst, I owe you an apology. This is my first update in two quarters. The numbers were flat and I didn't want to send bad news. That was the wrong call. From now on you'll get an update in the first week of every quarter, starting January 7. I'll also send a one-page set of numbers every month to anyone who wants it. Just reply and ask.\n\n**The numbers**\n- Monthly recurring revenue: $41,000, the same as three months ago.\n- Clinics: we added 9 and lost 4.\n- Cash: $480,000 in the bank. We're losing about $44,000 a month, so we have about 11 months of runway.\n\n**The loss that matters**\nOne of the four clinics we lost was our largest customer, a 12-clinic chain paying $5,500 a month. They moved to the scheduler built into their electronic records system. Revenue from new clinics made up for the loss, which is why revenue held flat instead of falling. But it also means this quarter's sales went into replacing revenue, not growing it.\n\nThe risk is bigger than one customer. Two other customers use the same records system and together pay $3,800 a month. I can't promise they won't leave the same way. I also don't yet know how many of our clinics overall use a records system that has its own scheduler.\n\n**What's working**\nClinics that use our automatic text reminders have a 7% no-show rate, down from 13% before they started using them. That is the clearest value we deliver today.\n\n**What's next**\nOn December 1 we start selling the reminder feature on its own for $150 a month. Six clinics have said they'll buy it at launch. If all six follow through, that's $900 a month. It's small, but it's our first test of whether reminders can sell on their own. I'll report how it went on January 7.\n\n**What I'm asking for**\n1. **20 minutes on the phone with each of you.** I haven't decided whether to raise more money or cut costs, and I'd like your view before I do. Please reply if you're open to a call.\n2. **Introductions to physical therapy clinic chains.** If you know someone who runs or manages operations at a multi-clinic practice, I'd be grateful for an intro.\n\nThank you for your patience over the last six months. You'll hear from me on January 7.\n\n[Your name]\n[Company]\n</final_document>\n\nA few things to know before you send it:\n\n- **Placeholders:** fill in your company name and your name.\n- **Things I left out because you didn't know them:** total clinic count, who the standalone reminder feature is mainly for, and a target for next quarter. Investors may ask how many clinics and appointments the 7%/13% figure comes from, so have that ready for the calls.\n- **Runway:** 11 months from now puts you at about October 2027. I didn't include the date, but you could add it if you want the deadline to be concrete."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1039,"cache_read_input_tokens":10169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1039},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b7e1fa-a687-41f1-b7c5-a0fbaf369a54","uuid":"244253a9-f4b4-4a7a-b0c8-9494f2d7a3f1","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:22:36.122Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7EHc6RFmaQpMEkcUyd6"}
